  "conclusion": "Moving GELU gates while retaining the dense c_fc normal field preserves 96.7% of analytic input-JVP energy, whereas freezing teacher gates while imposing the rank-480 normal field preserves only 23.4-23.8%. The normal term explains about 97.1% of exact tangent-error energy and the activation-boundary term only about 4.0%; their first-order sum explains about 96.1%. The principal failure is therefore the rank(c_fc)<=480 normal-field restriction, not GELU boundary phase. Low-dimensional parameter evolution does not imply a low-rank materialized c_fc. The next family must generate full-input-rank c_fc and must not spend the next experiment on a boundary-only loss.",
